recipe hotkey: a global hotkey: F8 toggles pause while another app has focus (Linux X11)

A key that works while the app is in the background: F8 pauses and resumes a recording from any
window. `j3.game.hotkey` grabs the combo on the X11 root window; `j3c doc j3.game.hotkey` has the rules.

- `hotkey.register(Key.F8, hotkey.NONE)` returns `Result<Hotkey, HotkeyError>`. Modifiers add up:
  `hotkey.CTRL + hotkey.SHIFT` (`SHIFT`, `CTRL`, `ALT`, `SUPER`).
- Poll `hk.pressed()` from the frame loop (main thread). It is true once per press; held keys do
  not repeat. A grabbed key reaches the hotkey even when this window has focus (SDL never sees
  it), so `hk.pressed() || game.keyPressed(Key.F8)` covers both the grab and the fallback.
  `Hotkey {}` is an empty handle that never fires.
- While registered, the focused app never gets that combo. Pick one people do not type.
- Errors: `Taken` (another app holds it), `Unsupported` (Wayland, no libX11, macOS, Android; Windows uses `RegisterHotKey`),
  `NoDisplay` (no X server, `--headless`), `UnknownKey` (not on this keymap). Fall back to the
  in-window key; never panic on them.
- `hk.unregister()` frees the combo; the X server also drops grabs when the process exits.
- Test the fallback path headless; test the grab by hand (another window focused, press F8).

==> j3.toml <==
[package]
name = "recorder"
entry = "src/main.j3"

[link]
libs = ["SDL2"]

==> src/main.j3 <==
module recorder;

use j3.app.App;
use j3.game;
use j3.game.{ Key, rgb };
use j3.game.hotkey;
use j3.game.hotkey.Hotkey;
use j3.gfx.paint;
use j3.io.printLn;
use j3.math.Vec2;
use j3.memory.Arena;
use j3.result.Result;

struct World {
    hk: Hotkey;
    paused: bool = false;
}

fn boot(mem: &Arena): World {
    return World { hk: Hotkey {} };
}

fn startup(w: &World) {
    // F8 works while another app has focus. Err on Wayland, headless, or when it is taken.
    match hotkey.register(Key.F8, hotkey.NONE) {
        Result.Ok(h) { w.hk = h; }
        Result.Err(e) { printLn("no global F8; using the in-window key only"); }
    }
}

fn input(w: &World, _dt: f32) {
    // a grabbed key goes to the hotkey, not the window, so the two never both fire
    if w.hk.pressed() || game.keyPressed(Key.F8) { w.paused = !w.paused; }
}

fn draw(w: &World) {
    let c = if w.paused { rgb(243, 139, 168) } else { rgb(166, 227, 161) };
    paint.rect(Vec2 { x: 0, y: 0 }, game.windowSize(), c);
}

fn main() {
    let app = App<World>.create("recorder", 320, 180, boot);
    app.useGl();
    app.startup(startup);
    app.always(input);
    app.draw(draw);
    app.run();
}
